    {
      "section": "Archive File 1",
      "unlock": "Unlocked at 50 trust",
      "description": "A towering female Oni. \nUnlike Madam Ch'en, she dresses very casually but easily reminds others of her post with her speech and demeanor. \nShe loves to drink, but no one has seen her inebriated to date."
    },
    {
      "section": "Archive File 2",
      "unlock": "Unlocked at 100 trust",
      "description": "As ranks go, Madam Ch'en is Hoshiguma's superior. But based on service history, Hoshiguma joined the L.G.D. before Ch'en and the two are long-time colleagues, so it's little wonder the line between them is almost invisible. \nWhat is unexpected is that Hoshiguma knows more about Lungmen then Ch'en. She has extensive knowledge about its criminal underworld, law enforcement, politics, economics, education, and foreign policy among others, and is unafraid to hold strong opinions about those topics.\nShe is indeed a rare combination of martial and scholarly talent."
    },
    {
      "section": "Archive File 3",
      "unlock": "Unlocked at 150 trust",
      "description": "Hoshiguma is no less aggressive than her kin in battle, usually the fiercest and most courageous on the field. \nHowever, she also possesses a quality most Oni sorely lack - composure. \nHer self-discipline is discernible in her speech and demeanor, as well as in battle. She has fully conquered the recklessness in her Oni blood. \nThis may have perhaps stemmed from her past."
    },
    {
      "section": "Archive File 4",
      "unlock": "Unlocked at 200 trust",
      "description": "According to L.G.D. record, Hoshiguma was already an anomaly even when was part of the criminal underworld. She never preyed on the weak, was always righteous, loyal and helpful, and could drink anyone under the table... In short, a throwback to the martial heroes of the East's long-forgotten history. \nIt's likely that these qualities allowed her to break tradition and gain a position in the L.G.D.\nBut it's also clear from the files that Hoshiguma is no different now than when she first arrived at Lungmen, so the question remains how did she manage to gain her composure and knowledge, and why did she work for criminals in Lungmen? \nEven if these stories took place before she arrived in Lungmen, she is still shrouded in mystery."
